text+=['','The 8 radial stress locations are deterministic 2x/4x extrapolations, not posterior samples. Trajectory locations are descriptively evaluated by both estimators, never used to claim posterior-average superiority. Four failure-prefix locations are stored checkpoints, not immediate pre-failure states. Reference locations are a small deterministic subset of finite reference clouds; no population-wide frequency estimate is claimed.','', '## Rare observations and Monte Carlo caution','',f"At the first reference location, the largest observation accounts for {ref[0]['cv1_top1_fraction']:.1%} of CV1 noise and the top ten account for {ref[0]['cv1_top10_fraction']:.1%}. Small Monte Carlo minibatch averages can miss such observations and severely underestimate noise.", '','The initial MC expectation check exposed this problem. The original diagnostic protocol and failure log are preserved. The finite-population factor was also corrected by N/(N−1), approximately1.000022; this tiny correction does not explain the much larger MC discrepancy. MC estimates/empirical standard errors are descriptive, not a normal-approximation acceptance gate. Per-draw estimator agreement and the exact covariance identity provide numerical verification. Original P3A sampler/results are unchanged.','', '## Original-stream failure replays','', '|Batch,h,seed|First failure|Checkpoint512 discrepancy|Radius before→after|Whitened drift|Whitened noise|Conditional noise ratio before failure|','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
